        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.568,
            0.847,
            0.627
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Example 7: A farmer harvested 260 kg of wheat last year. This year, they harvested 650 kg of wheat. What percentage of last year’s harvest is this year’s harvest?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.632,
            0.74,
            0.677
          ],
          "content": "This year’s harvest $\\frac{650}{260} \\times 100 = 250\\%$ of last year’s harvest. 250% indicates that it is 2.5 times the original value."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.685,
            0.295,
            0.707
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.705,
            0.847,
            0.745
          ],
          "content": "Estimate first before making any computations to solve the following questions. Try different methods including mental computations."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.747,
            0.845,
            0.768
          ],
          "content": "1. Find the missing numbers. The first problem has been worked out."
